@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@token = REPLACE_WITH_A_REAL_TOKEN
@tokenNoUpdateScope = REPLACE_WITH_A_TOKEN_MISSING_UPDATE_SCOPE
@tokenExcludedDeck = REPLACE_WITH_A_TOKEN_THAT_EXCLUDES_deckId_BELOW
@tokenNoSchemaUpdate = REPLACE_WITH_A_TOKEN_ON_A_ROLE_WITH_canUpdate_FALSE

### =========================================================================
### SETUP — root deck to hold every test card (copy the returned id into @deckId)
### =========================================================================
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/table
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "UpdateCardTestDeck"
}

###
@deckId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### SETUP — one text card with a real config (copy id into @cardId)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/card
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "CardToUpdate",
  "parentId": "{{deckId}}",
  "fieldType": "text",
  "defaultValue": "hola",
  "config": { "multiline": true, "maxLength": 300 }
}

###
@cardId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### =========================================================================
### 1) PARTIAL UPDATE — updating one field must NOT wipe the others.
### config and defaultValue must survive untouched (only isRequired changes).
### =========================================================================
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/card/{{cardId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "isRequired": true
}

### verify: config ({"maxLength":300,"multiline":true}) and defaultValue ("hola") are still there
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/card/{{cardId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### =========================================================================
### 2) EXPLICIT CONFIG UPDATE — per fieldType (same shapes as postCreateCard.rest)
### =========================================================================

### 2a) text: change multiline/maxLength
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/card/{{cardId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "config": { "multiline": false, "maxLength": 50 }
}

### 2b) number: fixed value
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/card
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "NumberCard",
  "parentId": "{{deckId}}",
  "fieldType": "number"
}

###
@numberCardId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/card/{{numberCardId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "config": { "subtype": "integer", "valueMode": "fixed", "fixedValue": 42 }
}

### 2c) number: switch the SAME card to a range instead
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/card/{{numberCardId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "config": { "subtype": "float", "valueMode": "range", "min": 0, "max": 100 }
}

### 2d) boolean
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/card
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "BooleanCard",
  "parentId": "{{deckId}}",
  "fieldType": "boolean"
}

###
@booleanCardId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/card/{{booleanCardId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "config": { "defaultValue": true, "trueLabel": "Activo", "falseLabel": "Inactivo" }
}

### 2e) gallery: replace items and maxItems entirely
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/card
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "GalleryCard",
  "parentId": "{{deckId}}",
  "fieldType": "gallery"
}

###
@galleryCardId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/card/{{galleryCardId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "config": {
    "maxItems": 5,
    "items": [
      { "url": "https://example.com/a.jpg" },
      { "base64": "iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAAAEAAAABCAQAAAC1HAwCAAAAC0lEQVR42mNk+A8AAQUBAScY42YAAAAASUVORK5CYII=", "mimeType": "image/png" }
    ]
  }
}

### =========================================================================
### 3) MEDIA REFERENCES — image/video updates (base64 upload, mediaId, url)
### =========================================================================

### 3a) create an image card with no default
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/card
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "ImageCard",
  "parentId": "{{deckId}}",
  "fieldType": "image"
}

###
@imageCardId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### 3b) set its default image via base64 (server uploads and creates a real media asset)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/card/{{imageCardId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "config": { "base64": "data:image/png;base64,iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAAAEAAAABCAQAAAC1HAwCAAAAC0lEQVR42mNk+A8AAQUBAScY42YAAAAASUVORK5CYII=" }
}

### copy the response's config.defaultMediaId into @existingMediaId to reuse it below
@existingMediaId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### 3c) point a DIFFERENT card at that same existing media, by mediaId (no new upload)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/card
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "ImageCard2",
  "parentId": "{{deckId}}",
  "fieldType": "image"
}

###
@imageCard2Id = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/card/{{imageCard2Id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "config": { "mediaId": "{{existingMediaId}}" }
}

### 3d) switch it to a plain external url instead (no upload, mediaId goes back to null)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/card/{{imageCard2Id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "config": { "url": "https://example.com/pic.jpg" }
}

### 3e) mediaId that does not exist → 404 MEDIA_NOT_FOUND
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/card/{{imageCard2Id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "config": { "mediaId": "aaaaaaaa-aaaa-4aaa-8aaa-aaaaaaaaaaaa" }
}

### 3f) setup: a video card with a real uploaded media, to test a type mismatch
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/card
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "VideoCard",
  "parentId": "{{deckId}}",
  "fieldType": "video",
  "config": { "base64": "AAAAHGZ0eXBpc29tAAACAGlzb21pc28y", "mimeType": "video/mp4" }
}

### copy the response's config.defaultMediaId into @existingVideoMediaId
@existingVideoMediaId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### 3g) mediaId type mismatch: point the IMAGE card at the VIDEO's media → 422 MEDIA_TYPE_MISMATCH
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/card/{{imageCard2Id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "config": { "mediaId": "{{existingVideoMediaId}}" }
}

### =========================================================================
### 4) RELATION — relationTargetId (top-level) and relationType (in config)
### =========================================================================

### 4a) setup: a real target deck and a plain text card to convert into a relation
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/table
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "RelationTargetDeck"
}

###
@relationTargetId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/card
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "ToBecomeRelation",
  "parentId": "{{deckId}}",
  "fieldType": "text"
}

###
@relationCardId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### 4b) change its type to relation, set target and relationType together (write both at once:
### changing fieldType without sending a matching config leaves the OLD type's config
### shape in place, so always send fieldType + relationTargetId + config together)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/card/{{relationCardId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fieldType": "relation",
  "relationTargetId": "{{relationTargetId}}",
  "config": { "relationType": "n:m" }
}

### 4c) relationTargetId that is well-formed but does not exist → 422 RELATION_TARGET_NOT_FOUND
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/card/{{relationCardId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "relationTargetId": "aaaaaaaa-aaaa-4aaa-8aaa-aaaaaaaaaaaa"
}

### 4d) relationTargetId that IS a real node but a card, not a deck → 422 RELATION_TARGET_MUST_BE_CONTAINER
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/card/{{relationCardId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "relationTargetId": "{{numberCardId}}"
}

### =========================================================================
### 5) FIELD TYPE CHANGE — allowed only while the deck has zero records.
### The public API has no "force change + wipe data" path (that only exists
### in the CMS board UI's own confirm dialog).
### =========================================================================

### 5a) fieldType change on a card with no records yet → succeeds
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/card
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "FreeToChange",
  "parentId": "{{deckId}}",
  "fieldType": "text"
}

###
@freeCardId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/card/{{freeCardId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fieldType": "number",
  "config": { "subtype": "integer" }
}

### 5b) setup: a card that DOES have a record referencing it (needs its own clean deck,
### so no OTHER required card blocks the record write)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/table
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "BlockedTypeChangeDeck"
}

###
@blockedDeckId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/card
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "onlyField",
  "parentId": "{{blockedDeckId}}",
  "fieldType": "text"
}

###
@blockedCardId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### create the record on the deck's own slug (equals the deck's simpleName: blockedtypechangedeck)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/blockedtypechangedeck
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "onlyField": "some value"
}

### 5c) attempt to change its type now → 422 FIELD_TYPE_CHANGE_BLOCKED
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/card/{{blockedCardId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fieldType": "number"
}

### =========================================================================
### 6) NAME COLLISION — renaming a card to a name a sibling already has
### =========================================================================
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/card
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "SiblingA",
  "parentId": "{{deckId}}",
  "fieldType": "text"
}

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/card
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "SiblingB",
  "parentId": "{{deckId}}",
  "fieldType": "text"
}

###
@siblingBId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### → 422 { "error": "VALIDATION_ERROR", "message": "NODE_NAME_TAKEN" }
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/card/{{siblingBId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "SiblingA"
}

### renaming a card to the name it ALREADY has is fine (not a collision with itself)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/card/{{siblingBId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "SiblingB"
}

### =========================================================================
### 7) NOT FOUND / BAD REQUEST — malformed or wrong-type ids, invalid JSON
### =========================================================================

### 7a) non-UUID cardId → 404 NOT_FOUND
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/card/not-a-uuid
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "isRequired": true
}

### 7b) well-formed UUID that never existed → 404 NOT_FOUND
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/card/11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "isRequired": true
}

### 7c) a deck id passed as if it were a cardId → 404 NOT_FOUND
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/card/{{deckId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "isRequired": true
}

### 7d) invalid JSON body → 400 BAD_REQUEST
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/card/{{cardId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

not json

### =========================================================================
### 8) AUTH — missing/invalid Authorization → 401 UNAUTHORIZED
### =========================================================================

### 8a) no Authorization header at all
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/card/{{cardId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "isRequired": true
}

### 8b) unknown/garbage token
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/card/{{cardId}}
Authorization: Bearer this-token-does-not-exist
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "isRequired": true
}

### =========================================================================
### 9) SCOPE — token has no "update" scope → 403 FORBIDDEN
### Generate @tokenNoUpdateScope in Settings → API with scope = ["read","write","delete"]
### =========================================================================
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/card/{{cardId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenNoUpdateScope}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "isRequired": true
}

### =========================================================================
### 10) TOKEN POLICY — deckId (the card's parent) is in the token's excluded list → 403 FORBIDDEN
### Generate @tokenExcludedDeck in Settings → API excluding {{deckId}} explicitly
### =========================================================================
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/card/{{cardId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenExcludedDeck}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "isRequired": true
}

### =========================================================================
### 11) ROLE — token's role has schema canUpdate = false → 403 FORBIDDEN
### Generate @tokenNoSchemaUpdate on a role whose Settings → Roles schema
### permissions have "Update card/deck" unchecked for this project
### =========================================================================
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/card/{{cardId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenNoSchemaUpdate}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "isRequired": true
}

### =========================================================================
### CLEANUP — remove the test decks (cascades every card/record/media created above)
### =========================================================================
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/table/{{deckId}}?cascade=true
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/table/{{relationTargetId}}?cascade=true
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/table/{{blockedDeckId}}?cascade=true
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
